OL,3,GNEWSALawyer sentenced to unpaid work
OL,4,Aover campaign of abusive behaviour
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn Aberdeen solicitor has been ordered
OL,7,Fto carry out 200 hours of unpaid work
OL,8,Fafter subjecting a woman to an 18-month
OL,9,Fcampaign of abusive behaviour.
OL,11,FAlexander Hutcheon, 71, admitted
OL,12,Fassaulting, stalking and harassing the
OL,13,Fvictim as well as demanding sex with
OL,14,Fher between June 2022 to January 2024.
OL,16,FThe pair had known each other for a
OL,17,Fnumber of years having initially met
OL,18,Fthrough his legal work.
OL,20,FAt the High Court in Glasgow, Hutcheon
OL,21,Fwas given a community payback order and
OL,22,Fput under supervision for three years.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
